{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448728-list-of-all-garou-oral-records-need-help","id":1448728,"title":"list of all Garou oral records - need help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-16T17:13:58-07:00","id":1448728,"title":"list of all Garou oral records - need help","content":"I am making a list of all known oral myths, legends, stories, records, etc. of the Garou. I know I am missing a lot. Please add to this list any you know. Please provide their names, a brief description, and then what sourcebook(s) it comes from. If there are any critical facts like when the oral record was first made, or who made it, be sure to include that.<br /> <br /> Obviously, we have the basic ones of the setting.<br /> <br /> <b>The Litany</b> (Corebook) - The great song of ages containing the traditions, codes and laws of the Garou. In its full form, it is as much an epic poem as a legal code. Chanting it in its entirety can take hours. To simplify matters, the Litany can be summarized in 13 basic precepts.<br /> <br /> <b>The Silver Record</b> (not sure where this was first mentioned) - The Silver Record is the official complete record of the Garou. All the great, glorious, honorable and wise achievements of the Garou as well as the inglorious, unwise and dishonorable failures are recorded in the Silver Record. If something happens that is important to the Garou as a whole, its tale is incorporated into the Silver Record, no matter what. No Garou claims to know the entire Silver Record, but it is believed that if all Garou who know parts of it were to come together, none of it would be missing. All tribes must agree as to what is worthy of mentioning in the Silver Record; it is one of the bonds that unite the Garou.<br /> <br /> <b>Prophecy of the Phoenix</b> (Corebook) - One of the earliest Garou legends which foretells the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> <b>Prophecies of Shadow</b> (Dark Ages: Werewolf) - A series of prophecies made by the Red Talon Song-of-Shadows around the year AD 1200. It describes one prophecy each for ten different tribes, primarily on the European continent.<br /> <br /> <b>The Dark Litany</b> (Book of the Wyrm) - The Litany of the Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> <br /> Then some obscure ones. I am sure there are many more scattered about in various sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> <b>The Apologues of the Wyld</b> (Possessed, pg. 64) \u2013 A collection of anecdotes, stories, and fables about the Wyld including references to Gorgons. The legends recorded here are often contradictory or nonsensical. Although the record is quite old, being contemporaneous with the Silver Record, relatively few septs today preserve this tradition today. Most popular with the Red Talons and Black Furies.<br /> <br /> Then records that may be limited to individual tribes. I was impressed that Tribebook; Silent Striders had a lot of stories mentioned. Too bad the other tribebooks did not include more of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Song of the Executioner's Weariness</b> (TB: Silent Striders, pg 15) \u2013 This story describes how the Children of Gaia and then the Silent Striders went to the Silver Fang kings to petition them to end the Impergium.<br /> <br /> <b>Dance of the Dragon-walkers</b> (TB: Silent Striders) \u2013 Short epic poem about a night time raid against Mokole that destroyed a half dozen eggs during the time of the War of Rage.<br /> <br /> <b>Lay of the Wyrm-Foes</b> (TB: Silent Striders, pg 17) \u2013 Decrees the priority of Wyrm foes to be defeated for the Silent Striders. First Banes, then Cult of Set, then Mages, and lastly Mummies.<br /> <br /> <b>Lament for the Undying</b> (TB: Silent Striders, pg 18) \u2013 Collection of information concerning Mummies.<br /> <br /> <b>Song of the Godwalker</b> (TB: Silent Striders, pg 20) \u2013 Silent Strider tales of Jesus Christ.<br /> <br /> <b>The Fate of Hamid Eggstealer</b> (TB: Silent Striders, pg 21) \u2013 A story of how a Silent Strider Ragabash hid from angry Wyrm creatures and Garou for a month by hiding near the Ka'aba in Mecca.<br /> <br /> I also know there are various stories told in the Players Guide, tribebooks, and other places that aren't given specific names. For example, the story the Children of Gaia tell of the slain cubs. If you want to add those, go ahead. Just make it clear it is unnamed, and give a brief name for it, like <b>Myth of the Origin of the Children of Gaia (unnamed)</b>.<br /> <br /> While I am not interested in the various versions of the litanies and stories of the other Changing Breeds, I don't mind them being included for the benefit of other readers of the thread.<br /> <br /> I know I am missing a lot, so please add what you know! I think this will help many others besides myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T19:01:31-07:00","id":1449301,"title":"","content":"I would add entire Garou Saga supplement, where you can find legends of different tribes, p. ex. Klaital's journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"",